      "title": "Days and Time in Korean",
      "title_kr": "날짜와 시간",
      "body": "Korean days of the week follow the Chinese five elements system: 월 (moon/Monday), 화 (fire/Tuesday), 수 (water/Wednesday), 목 (wood/Thursday), 금 (metal/Friday), 토 (earth/Saturday), 일 (sun/Sunday). Time uses Sino-Korean numbers for minutes and native Korean for hours.",
      "tip": { "icon": "📅", "label": "Time mixing", "text": "To say 3:30, Koreans say 세 시 삼십 분 — 세 시 uses native Korean (세 = three), but 삼십 분 uses Sino-Korean (삼십 = thirty). You must mix both systems when telling time!" }
    },
